From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally stop the firmware at
 reboot and power-off

The G16 driver has no shutdown path: the module is retained, and on a
reboot or power-off the firmware keeps running, the GFX domain stays
on and the GPU-to-fabric bridge stays linked until the reset. macOS
powers the GPU down at shutdown, and its PMGR driver unlinks the bridge
on that software power-down.

Register a reboot notifier for the G16 device. With g16_shutdown_stop
set (default 0) it closes publication and joins the poll worker as a
deep sleep does, then runs the same stop as the sleep's commit: the
firmware idled by polling, mailbox and run bit off, the bridge unlinked
when g16_bridge is set, the domain lowered. The waits are polled and
bounded. The stop is shared with the commit through one mapping helper.

Assisted-by: LLM
